pageKey: happyHour
title: "Tajima Happy Hour | San Diego"
description: "Happy hour at Tajima Ramen across San Diego. Times and what is on it vary by room, and Plaza Bonita does not serve alcohol. Walk in, no reservations."
---
{#
  /happy-hour/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.

  This page earns 1,361 clicks with ZERO internal links pointing at it. It
  catches 1,107 happy-hour clicks across 165 queries; all six location pages
  combined catch 32. A page nobody links to outperforms the entire location set
  by 35x, because "tajima happy hour" contains no location and a location page
  cannot answer it. The brief: "This must be in the nav. Its whole problem was
  that it was invisible internally."

  It is now linked from the footer, from /menu/, and from the Convoy address
  plate. FLAG: it is still not in the HEADER nav (nav.json primary), which
  currently holds Menu, About, Locations, and Noodle Room. Adding a fifth item
  is a design call on a header that was signed off with four, so it is Steve's.

  EVERY TIME AND PRICE ON THIS PAGE IS UNVERIFIED. See _data/happyHour.json.
  They came from the design concept, not from Tajima, and CLIENT_FACTS.md has
  no happy hour data at all. This is the same class of promise as opening
  hours, which CLIENT_FACTS.md forbids publishing unconfirmed, and it deserves
  the same treatment: Amanda confirms the table or the page does not launch.
#}

<section class="hh-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="hh-hero__inner">
    <span class="hh-hero__eyebrow">San Diego</span>
    <h1 class="hh-hero__title" id="page-title">Happy Hour</h1>
    {# Brief section 1: one line, happy hour runs at most locations and the
       details vary. Said plainly rather than promised uniformly. #}
    <p class="hh-hero__sub">
      Happy hour runs at most of the San Diego rooms. The window and what is on it are not the same everywhere, so the times below are per room. <a href="/locations/">Find your Tajima</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<nav class="hh-jumps" aria-label="Jump to a location">
  {%- for hh in happyHour.locations %}
  <a class="hh-jumps__btn" href="#hh-{{ hh.id }}">{{ hh.name }}</a>
  {%- endfor %}
</nav>

<section class="hh-grid" aria-label="Happy hour by location">
  <div class="hh-grid__inner">
    {%- for hh in happyHour.locations %}
    {%- set loc = (locations.items | where("id", hh.id)) | first %}
    <article class="hh-card" id="hh-{{ hh.id }}">
      <h2 class="hh-card__name"><a href="{{ loc.url }}">{{ hh.name }}</a></h2>

      {%- if hh.noAlcohol %}
      {#
        Brief section 4: "Plaza Bonita: no alcohol. Say it plainly."
        Quick-serve food court, no alcohol at all, per CLIENT_FACTS.md. Said
        directly rather than by leaving the card empty and letting someone
        drive to National City to find out.
      #}
      <p class="hh-card__no-alcohol">
        Plaza Bonita is quick-serve inside the mall and does not serve alcohol, so there is no happy hour here. The bowls are the same bowls.
      </p>
      {%- else %}

      <div class="hh-card__hours">
        {%- for window in hh.windows %}
        <div class="hh-card__hours-row">
          <span>{{ window.time }}</span>
          <span class="hh-card__hours-days">{{ window.days }}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      <div class="hh-card__lists">
        <div>
          <p class="hh-card__list-label">Drinks</p>
          <ul class="hh-card__list">
            {%- for item in hh.drinks %}
            <li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="hh-card__list-label">Food</p>
          <ul class="hh-card__list">
            {%- for item in hh.food %}
            <li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}

      <span class="hh-card__tag">{{ hh.tag }}</span>
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# ==================== PADRES ==================== #}
{#
  Brief section 3. Note the wording: "the San Diego rooms that pour it" rather
  than "all locations", because Plaza Bonita has no alcohol and the promo
  module in SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md excludes it explicitly.

  This is date-bounded in reality (a season, not a permanent fact) and
  SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md's position is that time-bound promos belong on GBP
  Posts. It is one block and it is deletable as one block, on purpose.
#}
<section class="hh-padres" aria-labelledby="padres-title">
  <div class="hh-padres__inner">
    <p class="hh-padres__text">
      <strong id="padres-title">{{ happyHour.padres.headline }}.</strong>
      {{ happyHour.padres.body }}
    </p>
    <a class="hh-padres__link" href="/tajima-east-village/">East Village is the walk to Petco</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="loc-close" aria-labelledby="close-title">
  <div class="loc-close__inner">
    <h2 class="loc-close__title" id="close-title">Pick a room.</h2>
    <p class="loc-close__sub">
      Happy hour is per location and so is the menu. <a href="/menu/">See the menu</a>, or <a href="/locations/">see all six San Diego rooms</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
